@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_A_REAL_TOKEN
@tokenNoUpdateScope = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_MISSING_UPDATE_SCOPE
@tokenExcludedDeck = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_THAT_EXCLUDES_deckAId_BELOW
@tokenNoSchemaUpdate = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_ON_A_ROLE_WITH_canUpdate_FALSE

### PUT /api/v1/table/{deckId} only renames a deck (name is the one field it
### accepts). There is no forceChangeFieldType-style endpoint for decks, and
### no way to move a deck to a different parent through this endpoint.

### =========================================================================
### SETUP — two root decks: one to rename, one to collide names against
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

###
@deckAId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckB"
}

###
@deckBId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### =========================================================================
### 1) SUCCESS — rename a deck
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckB2"
}

### 2) renaming a deck to the name it ALREADY has is fine (not a collision with itself)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### 3) NAME COLLISION — rename to a name a sibling root deck already has
### → 422 { "error": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "NODE_NAME_TAKEN" }
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### 4) VALIDATION — missing name, or a name with characters outside [a-zA-Z0-9 _-]
### =========================================================================

### 4a) missing name → 422 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4b) invalid characters in name → 422 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad@Name!"
}

### =========================================================================
### 5) NOT FOUND / BAD REQUEST — malformed or wrong-type ids, invalid JSON
### =========================================================================

### 5a) non-UUID deckId → 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X"
}

### 5b) well-formed UUID that never existed → 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X"
}

### 5c) setup: a card, to pass its id where a deckId is expected
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NotADeck",
  "parentId": "{{deckAId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@notADeckCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 5d) a card id passed to the deck-rename endpoint → 400 BAD_REQUEST "Node is not a deck."
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{notADeckCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X"
}

### 5e) invalid JSON body → 400 BAD_REQUEST
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

not json

### =========================================================================
### 6) AUTH — missing/invalid Authorization → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
### =========================================================================

### 6a) no Authorization header at all
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### 6b) unknown/garbage token
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer this-token-does-not-exist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### 7) SCOPE — token has no "update" scope → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoUpdateScope in Settings → API with scope = ["read","write","delete"]
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoUpdateScope}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### 8) TOKEN POLICY — deckAId is in the token's excluded list → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenExcludedDeck in Settings → API excluding {{deckAId}} explicitly
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenExcludedDeck}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### 9) ROLE — token's role has schema canUpdate = false → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoSchemaUpdate on a role whose Settings → Roles schema
### permissions have "Update card/deck" unchecked for this project
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoSchemaUpdate}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "RenameDeckA"
}

### =========================================================================
### CLEANUP — remove both test decks (cascades the leftover card too)
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckAId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckBId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
